= Footnotes <sec-footnotes>

A footnote stands where it belongs, in the middle of the paragraph.#footnote[This is what a footnote looks like: it stands in the text as a small number and is shown in the margin or below. When the paragraph is moved, it moves along.] It can contain text, citations and everything else that is possible in the text.#footnote[Citations belong there too, for instance @eco1977. Texts that are at the same time programs were called "literate programming" by Knuth @knuth1984.]

How footnotes are displayed you choose in the settings (Cmd+, on a Mac, Ctrl+, elsewhere): in the margin next to the text, as a list below the text, or as a card that opens over the text when you click. Try the three on this section. The numbers are the same in all of them, and in the PDF the footnotes are at the bottom of the page or, depending on the template, in the margin.
